From 53f7c6004f376438d8f39bb1ec5518d073d159b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gloria Yang <isotopxy@unc.edu>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:07:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add conversion layers to the map with card picker and
 view controls

- "Analysis dimension" becomes a card picker with two tabs: Over time
  (year slider limited to each layer's real years) and Latest snapshot.
  The existing rural-urban dimensions are unchanged and remain the default.
- Legend ranges are clickable filters; other countries are dimmed, not
  hidden, so they stay clickable.
- Country view: persistent 2D | 3D | World view control (3D by default,
  switching keeps the same country; the world overview is always 2D).
- Data tests (npm run test:data) for the published data and map helpers.
- Story card: "Learn more" button under the country name, and every
  value comes with a plain-language caption and the cross-country median.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
